//@version=6
// =============================================================================================
// US30 | 09:00 pre-open range break + EMA cross, 15-minute bars
//
//   THE RULE, all clock conditions in New York time, every decision on a CONFIRMED bar, filled
//   at the next bar's open:
//     range     the high and low of the bars from 09:00 to 09:30 (two 15-minute bars)
//     entry     AT THE LINE: a stop order resting at the 09:00 range high (long) or low (short),
//               filled the moment price trades through it, from the 09:30 bar until 10:30.
//               The order is placed on each confirmed bar while the conditions below hold and
//               cancelled when they stop holding. Two alternatives are inputs: a LIMIT at the
//               level filled on the retest after a close beyond it, and the original MARKET
//               entry at the next open after a close beyond it.
//     momentum  EMA(13) above EMA(48) for a long, below for a short (optionally: the cross
//               must have happened within the last k bars), read on the bar before the fill
//     trend     close above EMA(200) for a long, below for a short, read on the same bar
//     window    fills from the 09:30 bar to the 10:30 bar; unfilled orders cancel at 10:30
//     exit      stop and target in POINTS from the fill (100 / 100), flat at 16:00 New York
//     one trade per session, first fill wins
//
//   MEASURED on US30 15-minute bars, 2024-08-19 to 2026-08-26, 511 sessions, research = first
//   65% of sessions, locked = last 35%, 3 points round turn + 1 point stop slippage.
//   ENTRY AT THE LINE, stop resting before the break, EMA 13/48 + EMA 200 on the prior bar:
//     research (332 sessions)     263 trades   49.0% win   -1,442 pt    -5.5 pt/trade   PF 0.90
//     locked   (179 sessions)     151 trades   41.1% win   -3,117 pt   -20.6 pt/trade   PF 0.66
//     whole file                  414 trades   46.1% win   -4,559 pt   (-$22,795 on one YM contract)
//     vs a random entry matched on side, minute and block:  z 0.03 research, z -1.58 locked
//   ... plus the late rule when the conditions confirm only after the break (this script's default
//   is the retest):   retest  research 266 trades -2.1 pt/trade (z 0.58), locked 153 -17.8 (z -1.25)
//                     market  research 274 trades -6.5 pt/trade (z -0.13), locked 156 -19.4 (z -1.46)
//   ... with the EMA condition OFF (order rests from 09:15 on every session, trend gate only):
//                     research 305 trades -12.9 pt/trade (z -1.24), locked 169 -22.4 (z -1.80)
//   ... with NO conditions at all (every break, both sides):
//                     research 332 trades -4.7 pt/trade (z 0.40), locked 179 -8.7 (z 0.07)
//   LIMIT AT THE LINE ON THE RETEST:  research 123 trades -4.5 pt/trade (z 0.02); locked 84
//     trades +10.0 pt/trade (z 1.45, p 0.07). Better on the holdout than on research is the
//     wrong shape, and the bare limit-retest fill with NO conditions made +11.6 pt/trade on
//     locked by itself -- an execution effect of one regime, not the EMA cross.
//   MARKET AT THE NEXT OPEN (the original):
//     research 232 trades -10.1 pt/trade (z -0.84); locked 130 trades -23.4 pt/trade (z -2.20)
//     at ZERO cost it still loses 7.1 pt/trade on research and 20.4 on locked
//     neighbourhood swept: 16,200 cells on research, 0 beat the control at z > 2; the best
//     plateau (EMA 8/34, no trend gate, range 09:15-09:30, fills to 10:00, cross within one
//     bar, 100/100, flat 12:00) made 12.8 pt/trade on research and -8.1 on locked.
//     walk-forward: 2 of 9 folds profitable, stitched out-of-sample -24.3 pt/trade.
//   SECOND PASS, time held fixed, the rules widened (stop / limit-retest / fade entries, four
//   momentum variants, break distance, volume, range width, overnight gap, range-anchored and
//   break-even exits): 12,672 more cells, 13 beat the control at z > 2 where 41 would by chance,
//   none was a plateau, none beat its own bare entry mechanic. Nothing here is changed by it.
//
//   THIRD PASS, entry at the line, time held: exit management (chandelier trail 1.5x/2.5x ATR,
//   time exits at 11:00/12:00, half-off-and-trail, gap-fill target, 100/200), direction from the
//   DAILY trend (5-session momentum, 20-session EMA) instead of the 15m EMA 200, and whether the
//   09:00 range is the overnight extreme: 720 more cells, 0 at z > 2 where 11 would by chance.
//   No exit beats the plain 100/100 on this rule (research: 100/100 -5.5 pt/trade, trail 1.5x
//   -5.8, partial -5.9, time exit 11:00 -6.2, 75/75 -16.5, 100/200 -14.1). Best plateau cell
//   (close entry, daily-EMA direction, 100/100) is -1.0 pt/trade on research and -19.4 on locked.
//   Three passes, 29,337 cells: no configuration is profitable out of sample on this file.
//
//   READ docs/ib/STUDY_US30_ORB.md BEFORE TRADING THIS. The study's verdict is in that file,
//   and it is not "trade it".
//
// THREE THINGS THAT ARE EASY TO GET WRONG, AND WERE, HERE:
//   * Clock conditions go through an explicit timezone. Pine's bare hour/minute are EXCHANGE
//     time, and a Dow CFD or YM chart is not necessarily New York.
//   * ATR is ta.ema(ta.tr(true), 14), alpha 2/15, the research definition. Pine's ta.atr is
//     Wilder's RMA at 1/14. Only used when "size stops in ATR" is on.
//   * The chart MUST be 15 minutes. The range is the two bars stamped 09:00 and 09:15; on any
//     other timeframe the range and the EMAs mean something else. The script says so on screen.
//
// TICK-SETTING IMMUNE: entries require barstate.isconfirmed, so the Strategy Tester's
// "On order fill" / "On history bar tick" / "On realtime bar tick" boxes cannot change
// the result. Leave them on or off; the numbers are the same.
//
// NOT COMPILED BY TRADINGVIEW. A compiler error is a typo, not a changed strategy.
// Research tooling for education and analysis. Not financial advice.
// =============================================================================================

strategy("US30 | 09:00 range break + EMA cross", overlay = true, initial_capital = 25000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_order, commission_value = 2.50,
     slippage = 1, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false,
     process_orders_on_close = false)

// ---- clock ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tzIn   = input.string("America/New_York", "Timezone for clock conditions",
     options = ["America/New_York", "America/Chicago", "Europe/London", "exchange"],
     group = "Setup", tooltip = "Pine's bare hour/minute are in the EXCHANGE timezone. The research " +
     "is New York time. Getting this wrong runs the strategy an hour late.")
barMin = tzIn == "exchange" ? hour * 60 + minute : hour(time, tzIn) * 60 + minute(time, tzIn)
dayKey = tzIn == "exchange" ? year * 10000 + month * 100 + dayofmonth : year(time, tzIn) * 10000 + month(time, tzIn) * 100 + dayofmonth(time, tzIn)
newDay = dayKey != dayKey[1]

// ---- the rule's parameters ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rangeStartH = input.int(9,  "Range start hour",   minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Range")
rangeStartM = input.int(0,  "Range start minute", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = "Range")
rangeEndMin = 9 * 60 + 30                                  // the range always ends at the 09:30 open
entryMode   = input.string("Stop order AT the 09:00 high/low", "Entry", group = "Entry",
     options = ["Stop order AT the 09:00 high/low", "Limit AT the level on the retest", "Market at next open after a close beyond"],
     tooltip = "AT the line: a stop order rests at the range high/low and fills when price trades " +
     "through it. Retest: after a close beyond the level a limit rests at the level. Market: enter " +
     "at the next open after a close beyond the level (the original, and the worst of the three).")
winEndH     = input.int(10, "Last fill hour",   minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Window")
winEndM     = input.int(30, "Last fill minute", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = "Window")
lateMode    = input.string("Wait for the retest AT the line", "If the EMA/trend conditions confirm only AFTER the break",
     options = ["Wait for the retest AT the line", "Enter at market now", "Skip the day"], group = "Entry",
     tooltip = "The stop order can only rest at the line while the conditions already hold. On many " +
     "days the break bar itself is what flips the EMAs, so the conditions confirm at its close with " +
     "price already beyond the line. A stop placed then is below the market and fills at the next " +
     "open, which looks like a late entry. This input decides what happens instead.")
momOn       = input.bool(true, "EMA momentum condition on", group = "Momentum",
     tooltip = "Off = the order rests at the 09:00 high/low from 09:15 with no EMA condition; the " +
     "trend gate still applies if it is on.")
fastLen     = input.int(13,  "Fast EMA",  minval = 2, group = "Momentum")
slowLen     = input.int(48,  "Slow EMA",  minval = 3, group = "Momentum")
crossK      = input.int(0,   "Cross within last k bars (0 = EMA state only)", minval = 0, group = "Momentum")
trendOn     = input.bool(true, "Trend gate on", group = "Trend")
trendLen    = input.int(200, "Trend EMA", minval = 5, group = "Trend")
useAtr      = input.bool(false, "Size stop/target in ATR(14) multiples", group = "Exit")
slPts       = input.float(100.0, "Stop (points, or x ATR)",   minval = 0.1, step = 5, group = "Exit")
tpPts       = input.float(100.0, "Target (points, or x ATR)", minval = 0.1, step = 5, group = "Exit")
flatH       = input.int(16, "Flat hour",   minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Exit")
flatM       = input.int(0,  "Flat minute", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = "Exit")
allowLong   = input.bool(true, "Allow longs",  group = "Direction")
allowShort  = input.bool(true, "Allow shorts", group = "Direction")

rangeStart = rangeStartH * 60 + rangeStartM
winEnd     = winEndH * 60 + winEndM
flatMin    = flatH * 60 + flatM
modeStop   = entryMode == "Stop order AT the 09:00 high/low"
modeLimit  = entryMode == "Limit AT the level on the retest"
modeMarket = not modeStop and not modeLimit
lateRetest = lateMode == "Wait for the retest AT the line"
lateMarket = lateMode == "Enter at market now"

// ---- backtest window -------------------------------------------------------------------------
winMode  = input.string("All available history", "Backtest window", group = "Backtest window",
     options = ["All available history", "Last 90 days", "Last 365 days", "Last 3 years", "Custom dates"])
fromDate = input.time(timestamp("01 Jan 2023 00:00 +0000"), "Custom from", group = "Backtest window")
toDate   = input.time(timestamp("01 Jan 2030 00:00 +0000"), "Custom to", group = "Backtest window")
daysBack = winMode == "Last 90 days" ? 90 : winMode == "Last 365 days" ? 365 : winMode == "Last 3 years" ? 1095 : 0
inWindow = winMode == "Custom dates" ? (time >= fromDate and time <= toDate) : daysBack == 0 ? true : (time >= timenow - daysBack * 86400000)

// ---- primitives, defined to match the research exactly -------------------------------------------
emaF   = ta.ema(close, fastLen)
emaS   = ta.ema(close, slowLen)
emaT   = ta.ema(close, trendLen)
atrV   = ta.ema(ta.tr(true), 14)          // NOT ta.atr -- see the header
momUp  = emaF > emaS
xUp    = ta.crossover(emaF, emaS)
xDn    = ta.crossunder(emaF, emaS)
sinceUp = ta.barssince(xUp)
sinceDn = ta.barssince(xDn)
freshUp = crossK == 0 ? true : (not na(sinceUp) and sinceUp < crossK)
freshDn = crossK == 0 ? true : (not na(sinceDn) and sinceDn < crossK)

// ---- the 09:00 range, built bar by bar and frozen at 09:30 --------------------------------------
var float rHi = na
var float rLo = na
var bool  brokeUp = false
var bool  brokeDn = false
var int   tradedDay = -1
inRange = barMin >= rangeStart and barMin < rangeEndMin
if inRange
    rHi := barMin == rangeStart or na(rHi) ? high : math.max(rHi, high)
    rLo := barMin == rangeStart or na(rLo) ? low  : math.min(rLo, low)
if newDay
    brokeUp := false
    brokeDn := false
rangeOk = not na(rHi) and not na(rLo) and rHi > rLo

// bars whose CLOSE can decide something: for the market and limit modes the break bar itself
// (09:30 .. one bar before winEnd); for the stop mode the bar BEFORE the fill bar, so the
// order is live on the 09:30 bar (placed on the confirmed 09:15 bar) through the winEnd bar.
inSig   = barMin >= rangeEndMin and barMin < winEnd
inPlace = barMin >= rangeEndMin - 15 and barMin < winEnd
if inSig and rangeOk and barstate.isconfirmed
    if close > rHi
        brokeUp := true
    if close < rLo
        brokeDn := true

tUp = not trendOn or close > emaT
tDn = not trendOn or close < emaT
condUp = (not momOn or (momUp and freshUp)) and tUp
condDn = (not momOn or ((not momUp) and freshDn)) and tDn
longSig  = inSig and rangeOk and brokeUp and condUp        // market / limit: a close beyond it
shortSig = inSig and rangeOk and brokeDn and condDn
longArm  = inPlace and rangeOk and condUp                  // stop mode: conditions hold, order rests
shortArm = inPlace and rangeOk and condDn
ready = bar_index > 600 and not na(emaT) and not na(atrV)
isFlat = strategy.position_size == 0
oncePerDay = tradedDay != dayKey

// ---- entries -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stop and target are measured from the FILL, in ticks relative to the entry price -- the only
// Pine primitive that matches the research engine. strategy.exit tied to an entry id waits for
// that entry to fill, so it can be issued together with a resting order.
// barstate.isconfirmed is what makes this script immune to the Strategy Tester's "Script
// execution" checkboxes: orders are placed and cancelled at bar closes and nowhere else.
slT = math.max(math.round((useAtr ? slPts * atrV : slPts) / syminfo.mintick), 1)
tpT = math.max(math.round((useAtr ? tpPts * atrV : tpPts) / syminfo.mintick), 1)
if ready and isFlat and oncePerDay and inWindow and barstate.isconfirmed
    if modeStop
        // BEFORE the break: a stop order AT the 09:00 high / low, re-issued every bar the
        // conditions hold, cancelled the bar they stop holding. AFTER a close beyond the line
        // with the conditions confirming only now, the stop would sit below the market and fill
        // at the next open -- so the late rule decides: rest a limit AT the line for the retest,
        // enter at market now, or skip the day.
        lateUp = brokeUp and close > rHi
        lateDn = brokeDn and close < rLo
        if longArm and allowLong
            if not lateUp
                strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, stop = rHi)
            else if lateRetest
                strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, limit = rHi)
            else if lateMarket
                strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
            else
                strategy.cancel("L")
            strategy.exit("Lx", "L", loss = slT, profit = tpT)
        else
            strategy.cancel("L")
        if shortArm and allowShort
            if not lateDn
                strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, stop = rLo)
            else if lateRetest
                strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, limit = rLo)
            else if lateMarket
                strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
            else
                strategy.cancel("S")
            strategy.exit("Sx", "S", loss = slT, profit = tpT)
        else
            strategy.cancel("S")
    else if modeLimit
        // after a close beyond the level, a limit rests AT the level for the retest
        if longSig and allowLong
            strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, limit = rHi)
            strategy.exit("Lx", "L", loss = slT, profit = tpT)
        else
            strategy.cancel("L")
        if shortSig and allowShort
            strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, limit = rLo)
            strategy.exit("Sx", "S", loss = slT, profit = tpT)
        else
            strategy.cancel("S")
    else
        if longSig and allowLong
            strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
            strategy.exit("Lx", "L", loss = slT, profit = tpT)
        else if shortSig and allowShort
            strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
            strategy.exit("Sx", "S", loss = slT, profit = tpT)

// the moment a resting order fills: mark the session traded and cancel the other side, so an
// opposite fill cannot reverse the position
if strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0
    tradedDay := dayKey
    strategy.cancel("L")
    strategy.cancel("S")

// unfilled orders do not outlive the window
if barMin >= winEnd and isFlat and barstate.isconfirmed
    strategy.cancel_all()

// flat: the research exits at the close of the bar before the flat time; close_all on that
// confirmed bar fills at the next bar's open, the same price to within one bar's gap.
if barMin >= flatMin - 15 and strategy.position_size != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed
    strategy.close_all(comment = "flat")

if strategy.position_size != 0 and not inWindow and barstate.isconfirmed
    strategy.close_all(comment = "outside backtest window")

// ---- alerts, for a disciplined FORWARD test ----------------------------------------------------
// The only honest next step on this rule is new data. These fire once per bar close so the
// strategy can be paper-traded forward exactly as backtested: an order resting at the line,
// a fill, and the flat. Create the alert on "Any alert() function call".
if barstate.isconfirmed and ready and isFlat and oncePerDay and inWindow
    if modeStop and longArm and allowLong and not (brokeUp and close > rHi)
        alert("US30 ORB: buy stop resting at 09:00 high " + str.tostring(rHi, "#.#"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    if modeStop and shortArm and allowShort and not (brokeDn and close < rLo)
        alert("US30 ORB: sell stop resting at 09:00 low " + str.tostring(rLo, "#.#"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0
    alert("US30 ORB: FILLED " + (strategy.position_size > 0 ? "long" : "short") + " at " +
         str.tostring(strategy.position_avg_price, "#.#") + "  stop " +
         str.tostring(strategy.position_avg_price - (strategy.position_size > 0 ? 1 : -1) * slT * syminfo.mintick, "#.#") +
         "  target " + str.tostring(strategy.position_avg_price + (strategy.position_size > 0 ? 1 : -1) * tpT * syminfo.mintick, "#.#"),
         alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0
    alert("US30 ORB: flat, trade closed", alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ---- drawing -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(rangeOk and barMin >= rangeEndMin and barMin < flatMin ? rHi : na, "09:00 range high", color.new(color.orange, 0), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(rangeOk and barMin >= rangeEndMin and barMin < flatMin ? rLo : na, "09:00 range low",  color.new(color.orange, 0), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(emaF, "fast EMA",  color.new(color.teal, 40))
plot(emaS, "slow EMA",  color.new(color.red, 40))
plot(trendOn ? emaT : na, "trend EMA", color.new(color.gray, 20), linewidth = 2)
plotshape((modeStop ? longArm : longSig) and allowLong and ready,    "long armed",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.teal, size = size.tiny)
plotshape((modeStop ? shortArm : shortSig) and allowShort and ready,  "short armed", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.red,  size = size.tiny)
bgcolor(inSig ? color.new(color.blue, 94) : na)

// ---- what history this chart actually gave you, and whether it is the right timeframe ----------
var int firstBarT = na
if inWindow and na(firstBarT)
    firstBarT := time
var table dr = table.new(position.bottom_left, 1, 2, border_width = 1)
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(dr, 0, 0, "backtested " + str.format_time(firstBarT, "yyyy-MM-dd") + "  to  " +
         str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd"), text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
    table.cell(dr, 0, 1, timeframe.period == "15" ? "15-minute chart: OK" : "WRONG TIMEFRAME -- the research is 15-minute bars",
         text_size = size.small, text_color = timeframe.period == "15" ? color.gray : color.red)
